{"id": "q0425", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 3.9, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1607, "eot_read_ms": 28, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house", "transcript": "Provide a bulleted list of things to think about when buying a house.", "mode": "local", "answer": "Here are some things to think about when buying a house, keeping in mind that each step should be carefully considered to ensure you make the right decision for your needs and future plans:\\n\\n- **Budget and Affordability:** Determine how much you can afford by considering your income, savings, and other expenses. Don't forget to factor in property taxes, insurance, and maintenance costs.\\n\\n- **Location:** Think about where you want to live—proximity to work, schools, family, shopping, and amenities is crucial. Consider the neighborhood's safety, noise levels, and overall vibe.\\n\\n- **Type of Property:** Decide whether you prefer a single-family home, townhouse, condo, or another type of dwelling based on your lifestyle and long-term goals.\\n\\n- **Size and Layout:** Assess your current and future needs for space, including bedrooms, bathrooms, storage, and outdoor areas like a yard or patio.\\n\\n- **Condition of the House:** Evaluate the property's age, structural integrity, and any needed repairs or renovations. Consider hiring a professional home inspector.\\n\\n- **Future Resale Value:** Think about how easy it will be to sell the house in the future if needed, considering factors like location trends and market demand.\\n\\n- **Utilities and Infrastructure:** Check the availability and cost of utilities such as water, electricity, heating, and internet. Also consider proximity to public transportation or major roads.\\n\\n- **School Districts:** If you have or plan to have children, research the local school district ratings and options.\\n\\n- **Community and Lifestyle:** Visit the area at different times of day to get a feel for the community. Consider whether the neighborhood fits your lifestyle and values.\\n\\n- **Legal and Paperwork:** Understand the buying process, including contracts, financing options, and any legal requirements specific to your area.\\n\\n- **Timing and Flexibility:** Be realistic about how long you plan to stay in the house and whether your plans might change in the future.\\n\\nTaking time to reflect on each of these points will help you make a more informed and satisfying decision when buying a home.", "answer_ms": 13294}
{"id": "q0436", "pool": "easy-chat", "tier": "conservative", "audio_s": 3.04, "n_chunks": 4, "n_concurrent": 4, "gen_active_at_eot": true, "eot_score": 0.1374, "eot_read_ms": 24, "reference_answer": null, "query": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "transcript": "Why does Daenerys Targaryen want to rule Westeros?", "mode": "local", "answer": "Daenerys Targaryen wants to rule Westeros because she believes it is her birthright. As a member of the ancient Targaryen family, she sees herself as the rightful heir to the Iron Throne. Her journey is driven by a mix of destiny, prophecy, and a desire to bring change to a world she believes has been unjustly ruled.", "answer_ms": 1978}
